  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{偽|いつわ}る.\n\nUSAGE:\n{偽|いつわ}る is a formal, literary verb. In everyday speech, {嘘|うそ}をつく (to tell a lie) or ごまかす (to fudge/cheat) are more common. {偽|いつわ}る implies deliberate, conscious deception.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {名前|なまえ}を{偽|いつわ}る: to give a false name\n- {身分|みぶん}を{偽|いつわ}る: to misrepresent one's identity\n- {年齢|ねんれい}を{偽|いつわ}る: to lie about one's age\n- {経歴|けいれき}を{偽|いつわ}る: to falsify one's background\n- {気持|きも}ちを{偽|いつわ}る: to hide one's true feelings\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {偽|にせ} also appears in the noun {偽物|にせもの} (fake, counterfeit). The on'yomi compound {偽造|ぎぞう} (forgery) is a related legal term.",
